WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.412
Now the part that makes
the case for all this.

2
00:00:02.412 --> 00:00:07.638
Run the pull request check and it
passes cleanly: six rules, no findings.

3
00:00:07.638 --> 00:00:10.554
Then break a rule on purpose
by deleting the clause

4
00:00:10.554 --> 00:00:13.401
that keeps out empty worker
types, and run it again.

5
00:00:13.401 --> 00:00:15.100
Three things fire at once.

6
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.634
The linter flags the empty-slot risk,
the membership test for the worker with

7
00:00:19.634 --> 00:00:24.025
no type fails, and the shadow diff shows
exactly who the change would let in.

8
00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:28.370
Put the clause back, run the whole
suite, and seventy tests pass.
